From: SkiffOS <skiffos@skiffos.com>
Date: Fri, 04 Apr 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] HACK: arm: compressed: sun5i AHB/MBUS settle after cache_clean_flush

On Allwinner sun5i (R8/A13, C.H.I.P.) the kernel is completely silent
after U-Boot jumps to the zImage, even with the settle in patch 0006
(after decompress_kernel) and in patch 0003 (__enter_kernel).

Root cause: the decompressor calls cache_clean_flush() which writes
the remaining dirty D-cache lines to DRAM (up to 8 KB = 256 x 32-byte
lines) AFTER the main patch 0006 settle.  That creates a fresh AHB/MBUS
write burst.  Then cache_off() is called, which empties the I-cache via
"mcr p15,0,r0,c7,c7" (invalidate both caches).  After cache_off()
returns, the I-cache is empty: every instruction fetch -- including the
first instruction of our patch 0003 settle in __enter_kernel -- causes
an I-cache miss and goes to DRAM via AHB.  If the AHB write buffer
from cache_clean_flush is still in flight those reads stall
indefinitely.

Fix: insert a DSB + busy-wait immediately after bl cache_clean_flush
returns and BEFORE bl cache_off.  At this point the I-cache is still
populated from the decompressor's execution; the settle loop runs
entirely out of I-cache with no DRAM reads, giving the MBUS arbiter
time to drain the cache_clean_flush write burst.

  mcr p15, 0, r0, c7, c10, 4  @ ARMv5 DSB
  0x04000000 = 67,108,864 iters * ~3 cycles/iter @ 1 GHz ~= 200 ms
  r0 is scratch here (was the start-address argument to cache_clean_flush;
  not needed after the call returns).

After this settle, cache_off() and the branch to __enter_kernel execute
cleanly.  The existing settle in patch 0003 (__enter_kernel) then handles
any residual backlog before the jump to the decompressed kernel.

Guarded by #ifdef CONFIG_MACH_SUN5I.

Signed-off-by: SkiffOS <skiffos@skiffos.com>
---
 arch/arm/boot/compressed/head.S | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm/boot/compressed/head.S
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/compressed/head.S
@@ -655,6 +655,21 @@
 		mov	r0, r4			@ start of inflated image
 		add	r1, r1, r0		@ end of inflated image
 		bl	cache_clean_flush
+#ifdef CONFIG_MACH_SUN5I
+		/*
+		 * sun5i AHB/MBUS: cache_clean_flush() just wrote remaining
+		 * dirty D-cache lines to DRAM.  The I-cache is still populated
+		 * here; cache_off() will empty it.  After cache_off, instruction
+		 * fetches miss the I-cache and go to DRAM -- stalling if the
+		 * AHB write buffer from cache_clean_flush is not yet drained.
+		 * Settle while I-cache is still hot.  r0 is scratch here.
+		 */
+		mcr	p15, 0, r0, c7, c10, 4		@ ARMv5 DSB
+		mov	r0, #0x04000000			@ 67M iters ~= 200ms @ 1 GHz
+sun5i_flush_settle:
+		subs	r0, r0, #1
+		bne	sun5i_flush_settle
+#endif
 		bl	cache_off
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_ARM_VIRT_EXT
